+In the human view, the evaluation identity that every claim tuple names MAY
+be stated once on a page-level scope element in place of on each claim tuple.
+The scope SHALL be one element carrying a machine-readable scope marker, SHALL
+state the identity as text on that element in reading order before the claims
+under it, so that a reader without vision meets it once where a sighted reader
+does (PWB-REQ-016), and SHALL be emitted only when every claim under it has
+that evaluation identity in the machine answer. A claim that names a different
+evaluation invalidates the scope: no scope is emitted and each claim carries
+its own. A scope never overrides a claim's own evaluation identity, carries no
+other tuple field and no claim identity, and contributes no tuple of its own
+after expansion; every other field of the tuple stays on each claim. The
+machine answer SHALL carry the evaluation identity on every claim and SHALL
+not inherit.
